            <ArticleTitle>Distribution of diagnoses in a population of patients with temporomandibular disorders.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e35-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.oooo.2012.03.023</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S2212-4403(12)00316-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">The objective of this study was to describe the frequency of TMD diagnoses in a patient population for comparison with the available literature.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Five hundred twenty consecutive patients seeking TMD treatment underwent a Research Diagnostic Criteria for Temporomandibular Disorders (RDC/TMD) assessment. The prevalence and age distribution of the different RDC/TMD axis I and II diagnoses were described.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Muscle disorders, disk displacements, and other joint disorders were diagnosed respectively in 56.4%, 42.0%, and 57.5% of patients. Sixty percent of patients had depression symptoms, 76.6% had somatization, and 21.8% presented high levels of pain-related impairment. Disk displacements were more frequently diagnosed in the younger-aged, other joint disorders in the older-aged, and muscle disorders in the middle-aged subjects (ANOVA for mean age comparison, F = 3.355; P = .002).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">These distribution frequencies of TMD diagnoses provide insight into the epidemiology of this disease.</AbstractText>
